{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Ibn Majah","section":{"24":{"eng-name":"The Chapters on Jihad","ara-name":"كتاب الجهاد"}},"section_detail":{"24":{"hadithnumber_first":2753,"hadithnumber_last":2881,"arabicnumber_first":2753,"arabicnumber_last":2881}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":2877,"arabicnumber":2877,"text":"Rapporté par Ibn ‘Umar : Le Messager d’Allah (ﷺ) faisait maigrir un cheval pour la course, puis il lançait le cheval amaigri de Hafya’ jusqu’à Thaniyyatul-Wada’, et (il lançait) le cheval non amaigri de Thaniyyatul-Wada’ jusqu’à la mosquée des Banu Zuraiq","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}],"reference":{"book":24,"hadith":125},"chapter":{"id":44,"ara-name":"باب السَّبَقِ وَالرِّهَانِ","eng-name":"Competitions and contests","isFirstHadith":false}}]}